---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageMeta from '@/components/PageMeta.astro';
import GatewayCard from '@/components/ia/GatewayCard.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Concepts and architecture"
  description="Understand the conceptual commitments, identity doctrine, modelling lenses, graph separation and audience views of the schema-derived ontology."
>
  <PageMeta category="PDTF schema · schema-derived ontology" variant="brand" updated="Draft · under review" />
  <h1>Concepts and architecture</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Start here when the question is why the ontology is shaped as it is rather than where
    to find one term. This category explains identity, classification and dependence; the
    separation of class, validation and annotation graphs; the modelling lenses used to
    test those choices; and the reader-specific views generated from the same corpus.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--warn">
    <p class="callout__label">schema-derived draft</p>
    <p>
      These pages explain the architecture of a draft ontology extracted from PDTF schema.
      They are not an approved SPDTF conceptual model. SPDTF domain meaning remains
      subject to its evidence-up working-group and governance process.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="questions">Questions this category answers</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Question</th><th scope="col">Architectural concern</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">What kind of thing is this?</th><td>UFO-informed categories and the distinction between Kinds, Roles, Relators, Qualities and information objects.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">What makes it the same thing over time?</th><td>Identity criteria, with identifiers such as UPRN treated as contingent qualities rather than identity itself.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">What is inferred and what is checked?</th><td>Three-graph separation and the governed boundary between open-world semantics, SHACL validation and annotations.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">How should I read the model?</th><td>Concept, logical, deployment, ontology and relational views for different audiences and tasks.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="explore">Explore the architecture</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/concepts-and-architecture/foundation" title="Foundations and architecture" eyebrow="Core commitments" description="Read the three-graph separation, the UFO and OntoClean frame, the dct:source contract that grounds each term, and the inference-versus-validation boundary recorded in ODR-0004." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/concepts-and-architecture/identity" title="Identity and classification" eyebrow="Identity doctrine" description="Distinguish Property, LegalEstate and RegisteredTitle as three Kinds with three identity criteria; UPRN is a contingent Quality, never the identity criterion itself (ODR-0005)." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/concepts-and-architecture/foundational-ontology" title="Foundational ontology critique" eyebrow="Limits of the lens" description="See exactly how UFO and OntoClean inform the model, where their use stops, and which claims the corpus does not make." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/concepts-and-architecture/modelling-frameworks" title="Modelling frameworks" eyebrow="Compared approaches" description="Review the upper-ontology and modelling frameworks assessed for the extracted corpus and the recorded rationale for their bounded use." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/terms-and-model-resources/graph" title="Interactive graph" eyebrow="Visual exploration" description="Inspect the OWL class backbone as a filterable node-link graph, switch on the SKOS layer, filter by module, focus a neighbourhood and open detailed resource pages (ADR-0043)." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/model-views-by-audience" title="Model views by audience" eyebrow="Reader views" description="Choose a concept, logical, deployment, physical-ontology or relational presentation of the same underlying semantic corpus." />
  </div>

  <h2 id="one-model">One corpus, several views</h2>
  <p>
    The conceptual pages, interactive graph and model tiers are presentations of one
    committed corpus; they do not create parallel specifications. Use the conceptual pages
    to interpret modelling commitments, then use the <a href="/spdtf/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/terms-and-model-resources">term and model-resource indexes</a>
    for exact identifiers and the <a href="/spdtf/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/validation-and-examples">validation and example pages</a>
    for executable constraints and diagnostic cases.
  </p>
</Layout>
